      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals erred in holding that reversal of Respondent's conviction was appropriate on plain error review if there was any possibility, no matter how unlikely, that the jury's verdict was based entirely on conduct predating the enactment of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Are there errors that are -- that are so basic that they would call for an automatic new trial? You say this -- this is not such a -- such an error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you this? Prong three of -- of Olano looks to prejudice, right? And then it's your position that prong four also looks to prejudice? Where you have two prejudice inquiries, one is more searching than the other, perhaps?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Glenn Marcus",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do believe there are errors that are so basic that they require a reversal automatically. And certainly one of them is trying a person for conduct for 2 years that violated no law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FAHRINGER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FAHRINGER: Your Honor, as I know, you are aware of the Marks case. They held that the ex post facto concept applied to judicial precedent as well, and that was repeated in the Harris case in -- as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FAHRINGER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FAHRINGER: My argument is, Your Honor, that no person in this country under our Constitution should be tried for 1 day on conduct that did not violate a law. I -- I --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "41725085540a9204a5c18ed0005b81ee0a4d4272dcd5b94d6f6d08a9d3b7eba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-41725085540a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So your position is, essentially, plain error doesn't apply in this area; it's just error because it involved evidence pre-enactment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1341",
